# API endpoint notes (client package)

Health probes for the **versioned JSON:API contract** commonly live under **`/api/v1/health/live`** and **`/api/v1/health/ready`** (relative to **`/api/v1`**). If you keep a **`v1.yaml` mirror under** **`.cursor/api-documentations/openapi/`**, routing details usually match—it is **reference only**, not authoritative for typings shipped from this npm package.

Root aliases **`/health/live`** and **`/health/ready`** may exist for ops backends; they are not required when using **`baseURL`** that already prefixes **`/api/v1`**.

The client uses **`createHealthCheck`** → **`GET …/health/live`** relative to **`baseURL`** (**Mode B** typically already includes **`/api/v1`**).
